\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {DDR}{} as a function of perturbation strength $p$ for five graph augmentation families across three datasets: four label-agnostic operators (\texttt  {attr\_mask}, \texttt  {subgraph}, \texttt  {edge\_drop}, \texttt  {node\_drop}) and one prerequisite-preserving operator (\texttt  {prereq\_preserve}). Each marker plots the mean \textsc  {DDR}{} averaged across nine stochastic runs (three random seeds on each of three train folds). The families separate into a consistent ordering: $\textsc  {DDR}(\text  {attr\_mask})=0 < \textsc  {DDR}(\text  {subgraph}) \lesssim \textsc  {DDR}(\text  {prereq\_preserve}) < \textsc  {DDR}(\text  {edge\_drop}) \approx p < \textsc  {DDR}(\text  {node\_drop})$. At a matched per-edge budget, the prerequisite-preserving operator is strictly less disruptive than \texttt  {edge\_drop} on every dataset and strength.}}{20}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ddr-all}{{5}{20}{\DDR {} as a function of perturbation strength $p$ for five graph augmentation families across three datasets: four label-agnostic operators (\texttt {attr\_mask}, \texttt {subgraph}, \texttt {edge\_drop}, \texttt {node\_drop}) and one prerequisite-preserving operator (\texttt {prereq\_preserve}). Each marker plots the mean \DDR {} averaged across nine stochastic runs (three random seeds on each of three train folds). The families separate into a consistent ordering: $\DDR (\text {attr\_mask})=0 < \DDR (\text {subgraph}) \lesssim \DDR (\text {prereq\_preserve}) < \DDR (\text {edge\_drop}) \approx p < \DDR (\text {node\_drop})$. At a matched per-edge budget, the prerequisite-preserving operator is strictly less disruptive than \texttt {edge\_drop} on every dataset and strength}{figure.caption.26}{}}
